train:7574:s3,train,concept_gap,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,concept_gap,The student failed to understand the difference between simple and compound interest and did not apply the correct formula for compound interest.,eos,True,False,"The calculation of compound interest is incorrect. It should also take into account the interest generated by the interest. The correct formula is P(1+r/n)^(n*t), where P is the principal, r is the annual interest rate, n is the number of times interest is compounded per year, and t is the number of years of investment or loan.","### Analysis
