train:37193:s6,train,concept_gap,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,concept_gap,Final verdict: concept gap,eos,False,False,"When calculating the least common multiple of a group of numbers, factor each number into its prime factors. If there are any common prime factors after factorization, only the highest power of each common prime factor should be used in the calculation. Multiplying all the highest powers of the prime factors that appear will give you the least common multiple of the group of numbers.","The student's work shows the following calculation:
