train:17702:s6,train,concept_gap,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,concept_gap,The student's main issue is a conceptual gap in understanding the absolute value constraint |y| ≤ 13.,eos,False,False,"The error is in checking all possible combinations, which leads to the error. Since |y| <= 13, the possible solutions are 1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 11, 13. And since the absolute value is used, the value of y can also be -13<=y<0, so the possible combinations are 7*2=14.","### Analysis
