In the reference solution, it states that out of 20 people, 5 are left-handed women (since 1 part out of 4 parts of left-handed people corresponds to 1 part out of 5 parts of women, resulting in 1/4 * 1/5 = 1/20 of the total, which is 5 people).

The student's approach of multiplying \(\frac{1}{4}\) (right-handed people) and \(\frac{2}{5}\) (men) does not make sense in this context. This indicates a misunderstanding of how to apply the given ratios to find the number of left-handed women.

