val:36474:s5,val,concept_gap,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,concept_gap,This indicates a misunderstanding of how to calculate the loan amount in a hire-purchase scenario.,eos,True,False,"The equation is set up incorrectly. Since the borrower will pay off the loan in 60 installments, it will take 60/12 = 5 years to pay off the loan. Therefore, the interest for 5 years needs to be calculated. The correct calculation is 24000*(90%)*(1+12%*5) = 34500, and 34500/60 = 576.","### Analysis

