val:11753:s4,val,concept_gap,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,concept_gap,The student's method was fundamentally flawed because they did not correctly calculate the new perimeter after adding the 3 meters around the field.,eos,True,False,"The calculation is incorrect because the length of the barbed wire fence is not included. After adding the barbed wire, the total area becomes 56 * 4 * 3 minus the two exits on each side, which is 1 * 2 * 3 = 6. This gives us the correct total length of the barbed wire fence. Finally, multiplying this length by the cost per meter of barbed wire will give us the total cost.","### Analysis
