\[ \frac{350 - 225 - 15}{350} = \frac{110}{350} \equiv 31.43\% \]

The reference solution correctly calculates the profit percentage as:
\[ \text{Profit Percent} = \left( \frac{\text{Selling Price} - \text{Cost Price}}{\text{Cost Price}} \right) \times 100 = \left( \frac{350 - 240}{240} \right) \times 100 = 45.8\% \]

